---
title: "From shorts to search: 4 trends changing digital marketing"
description: "Four key digital marketing trends for 2025: AI-powered short-form video, TikTok's evolution into a search engine, the rise of privacy-first search, and how D2C brands win through rapid testing."
publishedDate: "2025-06-01"
category: industry
---

Digital marketing in 2025 is not the same game it was in 2022. Four trends are fundamentally reshaping how attention is earned and how leads are generated.

## 1. AI-Powered Short-Form Video

Short-form video (TikTok, Instagram Reels, YouTube Shorts) is no longer optional for consumer brands and is rapidly becoming relevant for B2B.

What's changed: AI tools have dramatically lowered the production barrier. A 60-second video that would have required a day of production in 2022 takes 30 minutes in 2025 with AI-assisted scripting, editing, and captioning.

**For B2B SMEs:** LinkedIn video and YouTube Shorts are the high-ROI channels. Authenticity outperforms production value — a genuine 90-second explainer by the founder outperforms a polished corporate video.

The format that works: "Here's a mistake I see B2B SMEs make, and here's the fix." Problem → solution → CTA. Under 90 seconds. No logo animation in the first 3 seconds.

## 2. TikTok as a Search Engine

TikTok's search behaviour is no longer marginal. A 2024 Adobe study found that 40% of Gen Z uses TikTok as their primary search engine for certain queries. Even in B2B, decision-makers under 40 are increasingly searching TikTok for vendor research, software comparisons, and professional advice.

**Practical implication:** Search intent on TikTok follows a different pattern from Google — it skews toward "show me how" and "what do you think of X" rather than transactional or navigational queries.

For B2B service businesses, this is an educational content opportunity. Short, authoritative takes on your specialist topic, posted consistently, build an audience that eventually converts.

## 3. Privacy-First Search

Third-party cookies are functionally dead. iOS tracking restrictions have made Facebook and Instagram audience targeting less accurate. Google's Privacy Sandbox, while delayed, is still coming.

**What works in a cookieless world:**
- First-party data: email lists, CRM records, gated content
- Contextual advertising: ads placed in relevant editorial environments, not tracked by user behaviour
- Google's Enhanced Conversions and server-side tracking for maintaining attribution accuracy
- Broad match + Smart Bidding in Google Ads (the algorithm does the targeting)

The SMEs who built their audience on rented social channels and third-party cookie data are most exposed. The ones who built email lists and CRM records are in the best position.

## 4. Rapid Testing as Competitive Advantage

The D2C brands that grew fastest in 2023–2025 weren't the ones with the biggest budgets or the best creative. They were the ones that tested fastest.

Weekly creative tests. A/B landing page experiments running continuously. Offer testing before creative testing.

**For B2B SMEs:** The same principle applies. The company running 4 offer tests per month will outlearn the one running 1 per quarter. Speed of iteration, not quality of initial guess, is the variable that separates the winners.

Start small: test your contact form headline. Test one email subject line variation per week. Test which blog post title gets more clicks. The compound learning effect over 12 months is substantial.

## The Throughline

Across all four trends, the pattern is the same: authenticity, speed, and first-party relationships are becoming more valuable while paid attention and borrowed audiences are becoming more expensive and less reliable.

Build what you own. Test faster than your competitors. Show up as a human, not a brand.
